From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:26:54 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: rebuild the own neighbor report when an AP follows
 its STA

An AP that shares a radio with a station interface follows the
channel of that station. When the interface is enabled, the start
call of the script retunes each started BSS and sets its beacon. The
own neighbor report then keeps the channel of the configuration, so a
neighbor report or a BSS transition request names a channel that the
BSS does not use.

Rebuild the own report of each BSS at that retune, as the channel
switch event does.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 src/ap/ucode.c |    1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/src/ap/ucode.c
+++ b/src/ap/ucode.c
@@ -867,6 +867,7 @@ out:
 				 hostapd_get_oper_centr_freq_seg0_idx(conf),
 				 hostapd_get_oper_centr_freq_seg1_idx(conf));
 
+		hostapd_neighbor_set_own_report(hapd);
 		ieee802_11_set_beacon(hapd);
 	}
 	hostapd_owe_update_trans(iface);
